  "Example 2 (3/13 pole pairs, 16 pole pieces): 1 of Fig. 17's 6 FEM points used for acceptance passes. The fundamental and 3rd harmonic of the 18 FEM points agree: 40.46 N m against 40.39 and -0.37 against -0.38. The differences alternate in sign from point to point: +27.5% at 3.2 degrees, -10.8% at 6.3, +5.7% at 9.5 and so on to +6.1% at 53.7, rms 1.02 N m. The model's ripple about the fundamental is at orders 45 and 51 a turn (0.84 and 0.76 N m), the 48 cogging periods of 6 inner poles against 16 pieces modulated by the fundamental. It is in antiphase with the paper's points. No rigid shift explains it (best 0.25 degrees, rms 0.97). The cause is open; a relative angle of the outer magnets and pole pieces that the paper does not state would move that ripple and not the fundamental.",
